  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n248.jpg">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/haochez"/>In His hand He holds the attribute of judgment. All believe that He is God of faith. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/habochen"/>He tests and examines hidden secrets. All believe that He tests the inwards. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hagoel"/>He redeems from death and delivers from destruction. All believe that He is a strong redeemer. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hadan"/>He judges alone those who come into the world. All believe that He is judge of truth. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hehagui"/>He is thought of as ‘<tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:exodus/3/14" type="quotation"><tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="3" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hehagui/quotations/quoted_exodus_3_14"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" n="14" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hehagui/quotations/quoted_exodus_3_14/14"/>I am that I am<tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/></tei:seg>’. All believe that He was<j:conditional xml:id="musaf_haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat_segment_5"><j:all><tei:fs type="opensiddur:variant"><tei:f name="urn:x-opensiddur:condition:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hehagui/vehoveh"><tei:binary value="true"/></tei:f></tei:fs></j:all></j:conditional>, is<j:endConditional target="#musaf_haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat_segment_5"/> and shall be. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/havaddai"/>Sure is His Name and likewise His fame. All believe that He is with none beside Him. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hazokher"/>He remembers those who remember Him in kind memory. All believe that He remembers the covenant. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hachotekh"/>He distributes life to all the living. All believe that He lives and endures. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hatov"/>He is good and acts well towards evil and good. All believe that He is good towards all. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hayodea"/>He knows the impulse of all creatures. All believe that He has formed them in the womb. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hakol"/>He has power over all and contains them all. All believe that He has power over all. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/halan"/>Almighty, He dwells in mystery, in shadow. All believe that He alone is He. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hamamlikh"/>He appoints kings and His is the kingdom. All believe that He is King of the world. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hanoheg"/>He leads with His mercy every generation. All believe that He retains kindness. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hasovel"/>He is long suffering and hides His eye from the stubborn. All believe that He grants pardon. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/haelyon"/>He is supreme and His eye rests on those who fear Him. All believe that He answers soft prayer. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n250.jpg" n="115"/><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hapoteach"/>He opens the gates for those who knock in repentance. All believe that His hand is open. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hatzofeh"/>He waits for the evil-doer and delights in his justification. All believe that He is righteous and upright. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/haqetzar"/>He shortens anger and holds back wrath. All believe that He is hard to anger. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/harachum"/>Compassionate, He lets mercy precede wrath. All believe that He is soft to appease. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hashaveh"/>He is just and treats small and great equally. All believe that He is a righteous judge. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:haochez_beyad_middat_mishpat/hatam"/>He is perfect and shows perfection with the flawless. All believe that His work is flawless. <tei:milestone unit="stanza"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
